WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:05.302
FLAb pulls together seventeen mutational landscapes
from distinct antibody families,

00:00:05.382 --> 00:00:07.480
drawn from eight separate studies,

00:00:07.560 --> 00:00:11.452
adding up to more than thirteen thousand fitness
measurements.

00:00:11.532 --> 00:00:17.923
Together they cover the six developability
properties that define a therapeutic antibody: expression,

00:00:18.003 --> 00:00:23.240
thermostability, immunogenicity, aggregation,
polyreactivity, and binding affinity.

00:00:23.320 --> 00:00:27.085
Each property is grounded in its own real
experimental unit,

00:00:27.165 --> 00:00:32.594
from micrograms per milliliter for expression to
melting temperature for stability and

00:00:32.674 --> 00:00:34.837
dissociation constants for binding.

00:00:34.917 --> 00:00:41.820
This diversity is what lets FLAb test whether a
model generalizes across the many facets of antibody fitness.
